#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073567 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073852 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bbf7f692-6019-55eb-9fc9-c4cad3c4df93" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Ratios From Tape Diagrams"}] :question/id #uuid "032ead48-0a3f-5a5e-b604-2a2fc0d91770" :question/math-academy-id "e-2288" :question/problem "The tape diagram below shows the ratio between small and big tokens in a desk game. What is the ratio of big tokens to all tokens?\n\n![](images/5b/5b779b66fb6e6717e102398153f09f3cb70582a4333a68ad2aeeb97fced47c9b.png)" :question/worked-solution "The tape diagram for big tokens shows $4$ boxes. So, there are $4$ big tokens.\n\nAltogether, there are\n\n$$\n12+4=16\n$$\n\nboxes. So, there are $16$ tokens in all.\n\nTherefore, the ratio of big tokens to all tokens is $4:16$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073569 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073853 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5ef376fd-9191-586d-b172-5e46e3043243" :knowledge-point/title "Creating Tape Diagrams Given a Ratio"}] :question/id #uuid "fe68a823-4477-5d82-bd17-12842d6e8735" :question/math-academy-id "e-2290" :question/problem "Abbie and Kate are making cupcakes. Abbie makes $5$ cupcakes for every $7$ that Kate makes. Which tape diagram represents the given scenario?" :question/worked-solution "We are told that:\n\n> Abbie makes $\\color{blue}5$ cupcakes for every $\\color{red}7$ that Kate makes.\n\nSo, in a tape diagram, Abbie's tape must contain $\\color{blue}5$ boxes, while Kate's tape should have $\\color{red}7$ boxes.\n\nTherefore, the diagram is the following:\n\n![](images/47/47c6e186cd17bffc7e83cca0c228bc1d05287cfba1bdb394c0a5dd71d411294a.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073574 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073854 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5aedad19-4881-5b53-9ec9-335bbe9cec48" :knowledge-point/title "Interpreting Tape Diagrams Using Multiple Units"}] :question/id #uuid "c089129a-f06b-53d3-a7be-d8d8a79b6dd9" :question/math-academy-id "e-2295" :question/problem "The tape diagram below shows the ratio between the number of orange plastic building blocks and blue plastic building blocks that Tom has. If there are $54$ orange plastic building blocks, how many plastic building blocks are there altogether?\n\n![](images/8c/8c05c3e85b33f385b2f4be02d57d1d34fdfcd94a6ca61b44411859d188f3d2cc.png)" :question/worked-solution "We are told that there are $54$ orange plastic building blocks. The tape diagram for orange plastic building blocks shows $6$ boxes. Therefore, each box in the diagram above represents\n\n$$\n54 \\div 6 = 9\n$$\n\nplastic building blocks.\n\nNow, we fill the number $9$ in each box of both tapes:\n\n![](images/16/16c543fb48a3d3c89c36b969cd4fceec36dd0c880664fd979c76740fd12c5722.png)\n\nSince there are $10$ boxes corresponding to the plastic building blocks in total, and each box represents $9$ plastic building blocks, the total number of plastic building blocks is:\n\n$$\n10 \\times 9 = 90\n$$\n\nSo, there are $90$ plastic building blocks."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073575 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073855 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "76a2f388-bfe6-567b-beec-c59644da1e8a" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Ratios From Tape Diagrams Using Multiple Units"}] :question/id #uuid "ca5d9154-4c7e-5866-a6eb-5e4c1fb4d24b" :question/math-academy-id "e-2296" :question/problem "A jar contains $60$ raffle tickets. The ratio of winning tickets to nonwinning tickets is shown in the diagram above. How many nonwinning tickets are in the jar?\n\n![](images/8b/8bdce5e82b4bcda74730503edebb9816d66175a1324784b11b9b08eeb17c9ba9.png)" :question/worked-solution "The tape diagram shows $1$ box corresponding to winning tickets, and $4$ boxes corresponding to nonwinning tickets. Therefore, the ratio of winning to nonwinning tickets is $1:4$.\n\nWe are told that there are $60$ tickets in total. The tape diagram has\n\n$$\n1+4=5\n$$\n\nboxes in total. Therefore, each box in the diagram above represents\n\n$$\n60 \\div 5 = 12\n$$\n\ntickets.\n\nNow, we fill the number $12$ in each box of both tapes:\n\n![](images/16/1669ac0d1aa6edd5bf53609121080dc8e8b685b57daa60b91daf3db816474ef2.png)\n\nSince there are $4$ boxes corresponding to nonwinning tickets, and each box represents $12$ tickets, the number of nonwinning tickets must be:\n\n$$\n4 \\times 12 = 48\n$$\n\nSo, there are $48$ nonwinning tickets in the jar."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186074472 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073852 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bbf7f692-6019-55eb-9fc9-c4cad3c4df93" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Ratios From Tape Diagrams"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9e9ba606-c993-5f55-84ef-a32b97de2fb3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5: 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186073071} {:answer/id #uuid "e51b772c-097e-5145-bdc8-c632e78c6ee1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5: 7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186073072} {:answer/id #uuid "702b7a97-6db0-5e9e-9476-eff81ca12bb8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7: 5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186073073} {:answer/id #uuid "72b73071-38f8-54a2-adcf-23cb43666286" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2: 5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186073074} {:answer/id #uuid "75184440-c4e4-53c5-bb2a-eb97fc6c2c4e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2: 7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186073075}] :answer-field/id #uuid "a1e07a1c-d165-5596-aedf-f135cce8a031" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186073070}] :question/id #uuid "6bb66df7-891d-5538-826d-40f885a0db34" :question/math-academy-id "q-61405" :question/problem "![](images/5a/5a5fd1